{
  "id": "u04-l06",
  "unit": "u04-food",
  "title": "Tastes & likes",
  "status": "draft",
  "tip": "To say 'I like X', Bengali turns the sentence around: **আমার মাছ পছন্দ** — literally 'to me, fish (is a) liking'. The person who likes goes in the **-র** form (আমার, তোমার, আপনার…). No verb needed!\n\nThe other way is **ভালো লাগে** 'feels good': **আমার ভাত ভালো লাগে** = 'I like rice.' Negative: **আমার ঝাল পছন্দ না**.\n\nHunger works the same way: **আমার ক্ষুধা লেগেছে** — 'to me, hunger has struck' = 'I'm hungry.' In casual Bangladeshi speech you'll hear **খিদা লাগছে**.\n\nTastes: **ঝাল** (spicy-hot), **মিষ্টি** (sweet — and 'sweets'!). Bengal is famous for its sweets: রসগোল্লা, চমচম, মিষ্টি দই (sweet yoghurt). **মজার** / **মজা** = tasty: **এটা মজার খাবার**.",
  "vocab": [
    {
      "id": "pochhondo",
      "bn": "পছন্দ",
      "tr": "pochhondo",
      "en": "liking",
      "notes": "আমার … পছন্দ = 'I like …'. Negative: পছন্দ না."
    },
    {
      "id": "lage",
      "bn": "লাগে",
      "tr": "lage",
      "en": "feels",
      "notes": "ভালো লাগে = 'feels good (to someone)' = like."
    },
    {
      "id": "jhal",
      "bn": "ঝাল",
      "tr": "jhal",
      "en": "spicy",
      "notes": "Chilli-hot. Also a noun: 'spicy food'."
    },
    {
      "id": "mishti",
      "bn": "মিষ্টি",
      "tr": "mishti",
      "en": "sweet",
      "notes": "Also the noun 'sweets' (রসগোল্লা, চমচম…)."
    },
    {
      "id": "moja",
      "bn": "মজা",
      "tr": "moja",
      "en": "fun; tasty",
      "notes": "Colloquial BD: খাবার খুব মজা 'the food is delicious'. Also 'fun'."
    },
    {
      "id": "mojar",
      "bn": "মজার",
      "tr": "mojar",
      "en": "tasty",
      "notes": "মজা + -র; before a noun: মজার খাবার 'tasty food'."
    },
    {
      "id": "khudha",
      "bn": "ক্ষুধা",
      "tr": "khudha",
      "en": "hunger",
      "notes": "Colloquial BD: খিদা (khida). Kolkata: খিদে (khide)."
    },
    {
      "id": "legechhe",
      "bn": "লেগেছে",
      "tr": "legechhe",
      "en": "has come on (felt)",
      "notes": "Used with ক্ষুধা: আমার ক্ষুধা লেগেছে 'I'm hungry'. Colloquially often লাগছে. Kolkata: খিদে পেয়েছে."
    }
  ],
